Source: pg-local-cache
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: maxbronnikov10 <bronnikovmr@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libssl-dev,
               postgresql-server-dev-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/profundium/pg_local_cache
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/profundium/pg_local_cache.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/profundium/pg_local_cache
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-local-cache
Architecture: any
Section: database
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${postgresql:Depends}
Description: transaction-aware PostgreSQL primary-key row cache
 pg_local_cache is a PostgreSQL extension that caches complete rows by primary
 key, with transaction-aware invalidation and an optional authenticated RESP2
 endpoint. PostgreSQL remains the source of truth.
